  "note": "First election under proportional representation. Uncontested by agreement between the parties: the Unionists rose from six members to eight, the Nationalists fell from twelve to five, and Sinn Féin won its first seats. Occupations printed in the source are not recorded. Calvert, Hughes and Loughran were members of the old council; James O'Reilly was reported as already selected as the new chairman."
